enerally, you'd be better to read actual Wikipedia on myths and legends - as Scion setting do not have very defined setting, it's basiclly 'setting is what Pantheons we use and GM says is in it'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myth_(disambiguation\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myth_(disambiguation</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-26-2024, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T21:30:45-07:00","id":1542665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aligena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1542640-information-for-a-non-scion-player?p=1542653#post1542653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are multiple websites about it. Just do a Google or whatever search engine you prefer search online for it. There is even some wikis about it if you look. Hope this helps!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just Google it&quot; is pretty much the definition of an unhelpful answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T21:39:15-07:00","id":1542666,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but that worked for me. I am sorry if it came off as unhelpful. It was not my intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28593-aligena","name":"aligena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T07:26:55-07:00","id":1542683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aligena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1542640-information-for-a-non-scion-player?p=1542666#post1542666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but that worked for me. I am sorry if it came off as unhelpful. It was not my intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response was less than helpful, so please allow me to educate you a bit. First, I've already googled it, hence my opening comment of having videos on the subject and looking for supplemental knowledge.<br /> <br /> Second: I've got a video on character creation from a source I trust but who doesn't know Scion very well that says you get 6 / 4 / 2 to distribute how you want, and 2 points to spread between the 3 attribute points of your favored approach (which seems very low). I've got another video saying the 6 / 4 / 2 but every attribute in the favored approach gets 2 points but I'm not familiar with that video maker, but it's the same number of points you get as in Curseborne so I'm inclined to believe it could be correct. I've got a couple of websites that say &quot;spend 18 points on attributes&quot; (same number as previous video but no distribution rules) which is the only thing I have multiple sources agreeing on, but it seems wrong, given everything I know about the other white wolf games and what I know of Story Path Ultra from Cureseborne previews it's almost certainly wrong. If I could find any pre-made legal characters I could count their attribute dots and check their distribution, but apparently no one makes and publishes starter characters, ever. (Which boggles my mind because character creation is how I tend to teach myself a new system, hell I've made a Curseborne character and that system isn't even released yet, and I'm willing to bet I've got it at least 95% legal.)<br /> <br /> And that's just for attributes, which has a definitive right answer. I doubt things will be easier to sort through if I want to dive into the magic system or the setting. Hence why I turn to the official forums for the game for support. If someone here has a site they recommend then I'm more inclined to believe it's information is legitimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}